WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.520
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:05.790 --> 00:07.630
♫Turtle, turtle, turtle♫

3
00:07.660 --> 00:09.680
♫Turtle, turtle, turtle♫

4
00:09.700 --> 00:11.330
♫Turtles have four legs♫

5
00:11.350 --> 00:12.970
♫Four feet walking along♫

6
00:12.990 --> 00:14.900
♫Popping its head in and out♫

7
00:14.930 --> 00:15.610
What's wrong, Grandpa?

8
00:16.430 --> 00:18.560
Has the turtle shell been preventing blood flow to your brain?

9
00:18.720 --> 00:21.210
I'm trying to act cute

10
00:21.230 --> 00:23.010
so you will stop being mad at me.

11
00:23.030 --> 00:24.770
Are you still mad at me?

12
00:27.330 --> 00:28.030
Whatever.

13
00:28.380 --> 00:30.320
I will handle what I did

14
00:31.410 --> 00:32.890
to your mother myself.

15
00:33.250 --> 00:36.410
But can we deal with Gaysorn's situation first?

16
00:36.550 --> 00:37.910
You’d better keep your word,

17
00:38.190 --> 00:39.530
or you'll end up with an even uglier costume.

18
00:40.890 --> 00:41.560
Fine.

19
00:41.900 --> 00:43.370
Where have you been?

20
00:43.530 --> 00:44.730
Hey, what is that envelope?

21
00:45.970 --> 00:47.900
I signed a property purchase agreement with Mr. Sompong.

22
00:49.750 --> 00:51.320
What, Grandpa?

23
00:52.010 --> 00:54.160
Of course I'll help you find Grandma Gaysorn.

24
00:54.400 --> 00:55.750
We still have two months left.

25
00:56.090 --> 00:57.190
We'll find her.

26
00:58.370 --> 01:00.350
Do you have any keepsakes

27
01:00.370 --> 01:02.280
that might be connected to Grandma Gaysorn?

28
01:02.300 --> 01:03.250
No, I do not.

29
01:03.360 --> 01:05.580
Your granny was insanely jealous.

30
01:05.600 --> 01:06.710
One day,

31
01:06.910 --> 01:10.880
she found out I had a jade ring that matched Gaysorn's.

32
01:11.000 --> 01:12.460
She snatched it

33
01:12.480 --> 01:15.010
and crushed it as if it were a rice cracker!

34
01:15.030 --> 01:15.920
Whoa...

35
01:16.390 --> 01:17.250
Granny was very scary, huh?

36
01:17.270 --> 01:18.220
She was!

37
01:20.750 --> 01:21.250
Mm.

38
01:26.160 --> 01:27.500
Oh, hey!

39
01:28.240 --> 01:29.630
Why did you bang your head against the door?

40
01:29.650 --> 01:30.160
Hey,

41
01:30.390 --> 01:31.870
you don't have to knock at this point.

42
01:31.890 --> 01:33.270
I knocked to let you know I was coming in.

43
01:33.289 --> 01:36.039
I can't imagine opening the door and seeing your little eggies on display.

44
01:36.960 --> 01:39.150
Can you stop saying "little eggy" already?

45
01:39.170 --> 01:40.950
You said it so much that Duidui started mocking me,

46
01:40.970 --> 01:42.470
"Little Eggy, Little Eggy."

47
01:42.490 --> 01:44.070
Everyone in this dorm calls me that now.

48
01:44.090 --> 01:45.130
Ugh, stop talking already.

49
01:45.150 --> 01:46.500
I have some news for you.

50
01:46.520 --> 01:47.070
Yeah?

51
01:47.090 --> 01:50.300
There's a tenant who said he's Grandma Gaysorn's relative!

52
01:53.900 --> 01:54.350
Really?

53
01:54.370 --> 01:55.100
Yeah!

54
01:55.240 --> 01:57.250
Little Eggy, you're happy, huh?

55
02:00.610 --> 02:01.890
Little Eggy.

56
02:05.900 --> 02:06.830
I will finally get to meet her...

57
02:08.470 --> 02:09.479
Why are you acting so nonchalant?

58
02:09.500 --> 02:10.330
Aren't you happy?

59
02:10.699 --> 02:12.270
I am, but I don't wanna show it.

60
02:18.130 --> 02:21.660
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

61
02:21.680 --> 02:25.940
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

62
02:27.960 --> 02:34.860
♫Every step we take has a meaning♫

63
02:34.880 --> 02:40.780
♫No path is ever meaningless♫

64
02:42.290 --> 02:48.610
♫As long as our hearts keep searching♫

65
02:49.380 --> 02:53.860
♫One day, we'll find what we're yearning for♫

66
02:53.880 --> 02:57.510
♫Walking alone is fine, but it's better when you're by my side♫

67
02:57.530 --> 03:01.100
♫It won't be lonely when you're here to walk beside♫

68
03:01.120 --> 03:04.040
♫Like a love that waits, waits at the D Dorm♫

69
03:04.690 --> 03:07.150
♫Like a love that remains, remains at the dorm♫

70
03:07.170 --> 03:14.050
♫Meaningful love and good things await on every path♫

71
03:14.070 --> 03:21.250
♫It might not be a coincidence that we get to meet♫

72
03:21.270 --> 03:28.450
♫There might be hidden meanings on the path beneath our feet♫

73
03:28.470 --> 03:35.670
♫Perhaps the D Dorm is what led me to meet you♫

74
03:35.700 --> 03:39.480
[The D Dorm]

75
03:39.500 --> 03:41.380
Hello, everyone.

76
03:41.400 --> 03:43.350
Today, I'm back at

77
03:43.920 --> 03:46.520
the D Dorm!

78
03:48.090 --> 03:51.040
[Dom, occupation: YouTuber]

79
03:51.240 --> 03:52.700
- Here he comes. - Oh, look, a celebrity.

80
03:53.440 --> 03:54.140
Guard Dum,

81
03:54.160 --> 03:54.870
Handyman Daeng,

82
03:54.890 --> 03:55.510
where is he?

83
03:55.960 --> 03:56.910
Where is Grandma Gaysorn's relative?

84
03:57.280 --> 03:59.190
Mr. Dom is standing right there.

85
03:59.410 --> 04:02.050
When I returned to my old house in Chiang Mai,

86
04:02.070 --> 04:04.360
I discovered something.

87
04:04.530 --> 04:05.660
Today's episode

88
04:05.680 --> 04:07.760
will be a special episode

89
04:07.780 --> 04:09.450
that focuses on

90
04:09.470 --> 04:11.890
my grandma's love life!

91
04:13.520 --> 04:15.040
That's right. This episode will...

92
04:15.060 --> 04:17.050
be about my grandma's

93
04:17.079 --> 04:19.070
first love.

94
04:19.240 --> 04:20.670
Will I be able to complete this mission?

95
04:20.690 --> 04:22.230
Stay tuned to find out.

96
04:22.250 --> 04:23.460
Ugh...

97
04:23.480 --> 04:24.760
he's a YouTuber.

98
04:24.880 --> 04:26.120
This is gonna be a headache.

99
04:26.500 --> 04:27.670
I'm sick of these camera addicts.

100
04:27.690 --> 04:28.670
Hang in there, okay?

101
04:29.170 --> 04:31.050
Hello, my name is Dom.

102
04:31.070 --> 04:32.530
Mr. Dobby, can you say hi to the camera?

103
04:32.740 --> 04:33.790
Hello, I'm Dobby.

104
04:33.810 --> 04:34.780
I'm the owner of this dorm,

105
04:34.800 --> 04:36.270
and I currently work as a freelance host.

106
04:36.290 --> 04:37.390
Feel free to contact me at

107
04:37.409 --> 04:38.430
062-41...

108
04:38.450 --> 04:39.740
- Hey! - Hey!

109
04:39.760 --> 04:41.360
You just can't stay away from a mic!

110
04:41.740 --> 04:43.300
Gotta seize the opportunity.

111
04:43.320 --> 04:44.020
Isn't this a bit much?

112
04:44.400 --> 04:45.470
Feel free to contact me.

113
04:45.980 --> 04:48.280
- Mr. Dom, so you're Grandma Gaysorn's relative. - Yes.

114
04:48.310 --> 04:50.270
My grandpa's first love.

115
04:50.500 --> 04:52.140
Do you have anything to back that up?

116
04:52.159 --> 04:52.650
Like...

117
04:52.670 --> 04:53.700
Even a photo of her would do.

118
04:53.720 --> 04:54.770
- Yeah, yeah. - Mm.

119
04:55.070 --> 04:56.270
A photograph...

120
04:56.570 --> 04:57.320
I'm afraid I don't have one.

121
04:57.340 --> 04:58.300
- What? - Huh?

122
04:58.320 --> 04:58.670
What?

123
04:58.840 --> 05:00.680
Hey, if you don't even have her photo,

124
05:00.700 --> 05:02.480
how am I supposed to believe you?

125
05:02.500 --> 05:03.880
- Yeah, that's right. - Mm.

126
05:04.200 --> 05:05.870
I have other proof, though.

127
05:06.180 --> 05:06.800
Oh?

128
05:11.700 --> 05:12.290
Here.

129
05:12.330 --> 05:13.060
- Whoa. - Huh?

130
05:13.980 --> 05:15.140
- Uh... - Um...

131
05:15.160 --> 05:16.140
I'm sorry.

132
05:16.340 --> 05:17.280
You mean this tissue box?

133
05:17.300 --> 05:17.870
No,

134
05:18.890 --> 05:20.680
I brought this out for everyone to see.

135
05:20.900 --> 05:23.520
Because once you see what I’ve prepared,

136
05:23.700 --> 05:24.750
I guarantee

137
05:24.770 --> 05:26.940
you'll cry your eyes out.

138
05:28.140 --> 05:29.870
Here it is, T-REX tissue! [They have great chemistry, though]

139
05:30.090 --> 05:31.050
Thick, tough,

140
05:31.070 --> 05:33.830
and soft like a newborn dinosaur's butt.

141
05:33.850 --> 05:36.240
T-REX tissue, shoo, shoo, shoo...

142
05:36.520 --> 05:37.500
Ugh!

143
05:37.520 --> 05:38.990
Why are we in an ad break?

144
05:39.010 --> 05:39.940
Where is it?

145
05:39.960 --> 05:42.390
The proof you mentioned. Just show us already.

146
05:42.409 --> 05:43.520
- Yeah. - That's right!

147
05:43.720 --> 05:44.530
I have it here.

148
05:46.800 --> 05:47.650
This is the real thing.

149
05:49.409 --> 05:50.670
Ta-da!

150
05:50.690 --> 05:51.470
Huh?

151
05:57.680 --> 06:00.810
This is something my grandma kept.

152
06:02.060 --> 06:02.780
Exactly!

153
06:03.040 --> 06:06.480
I gave this photo to Gaysorn myself.

154
06:11.300 --> 06:12.700
Oh, is this Gramps when he was young?

155
06:12.720 --> 06:14.250
- Mm. - Hey, he's pretty handsome.

156
06:14.270 --> 06:15.330
He looks like Monkan Kaenkoon.

157
06:17.840 --> 06:18.600
Huh?

158
06:18.810 --> 06:19.860
There's a poem, too.

159
06:20.500 --> 06:25.520
"Your smile is as sweet as honey.

160
06:27.340 --> 06:32.760
I am completely smitten.

161
06:33.810 --> 06:38.500
I lie on my bed with you in my mind.

162
06:38.930 --> 06:40.280
Oh, how will my weenie..."

163
06:40.300 --> 06:41.360
- Huh?! - What?!

164
06:41.610 --> 06:42.640
What kind of poem is this?

165
06:42.760 --> 06:44.250
Did he really write that?

166
06:44.270 --> 06:45.330
[Oh, how will my dreamy love reach you?]

167
06:46.040 --> 06:46.980
Dreamy love!

168
06:47.000 --> 06:49.070
- Yeah. - Oh, I see...

169
06:49.420 --> 06:54.500
"Oh, how will my dreamy love reach you?"

170
06:56.130 --> 06:57.200
What a weirdo.

171
06:57.760 --> 06:58.670
Dreamy love, huh?

172
06:59.300 --> 07:01.500
That kind of expression sounded cool back then,

173
07:01.520 --> 07:02.760
alright?

174
07:03.660 --> 07:05.690
Do you remember your grandpa's handwriting?

175
07:05.870 --> 07:07.070
Because if not...

176
07:07.200 --> 07:09.240
Wait, you have more evidence?

177
07:09.850 --> 07:10.460
You can use this!

178
07:10.480 --> 07:12.500
Ginkgo candy from the Qilin Pushing Veggie Cart brand.

179
07:12.520 --> 07:13.390
Nourish your brain

180
07:13.410 --> 07:14.880
and keep Alzheimer's at bay.

181
07:15.090 --> 07:15.880
Try the ginkgo candy

182
07:15.900 --> 07:20.050
from the Qilin Pushing Veggie Cart brand now, now, now....

183
07:20.380 --> 07:22.060
This really is Gramps' handwriting.

184
07:22.080 --> 07:22.670
Hm?

185
07:22.920 --> 07:24.840
- I remember his handwriting. - Yes, yes.

186
07:24.860 --> 07:26.250
It really is his handwriting!

187
07:26.270 --> 07:27.240
That's right!

188
07:29.140 --> 07:29.850
Mr. Dom.

189
07:29.870 --> 07:30.500
Yes?

190
07:31.810 --> 07:33.050
Is Grandma Gaysorn...

191
07:34.520 --> 07:35.690
still alive?

192
07:48.490 --> 07:49.050
She is.

193
07:49.070 --> 07:50.230
- Oh, yes! - Wow!

194
07:54.650 --> 07:57.840
My grandmother has always wanted to see her first love once more.

195
07:59.690 --> 08:02.100
Don't miss what happens next tomorrow.

196
08:02.120 --> 08:04.360
And don't forget to like, share, and subscribe to...

197
08:04.380 --> 08:05.850
the 'DODOMDI' channel!

198
08:05.870 --> 08:07.680
That's it for today!

199
08:07.700 --> 08:08.660
Bye-bye.

200
08:08.680 --> 08:09.110
Bye-bye.

201
08:09.130 --> 08:10.460
- Everyone, say goodbye to the camera. - Bye-bye.

202
08:10.480 --> 08:11.590
Please submarine.

203
08:11.610 --> 08:12.310
- Hey, subscribe. - Subscribe.

204
08:12.330 --> 08:13.360
Subscribe.

205
08:13.490 --> 08:15.240
- I've never been a YouTuber before. - Subscribe.

206
08:15.260 --> 08:16.470
- Subscribe. - Alright,

207
08:16.490 --> 08:17.330
see you.

208
08:17.620 --> 08:20.640
You had better prepare to burn me a new outfit.

209
08:20.660 --> 08:22.060
Make it a handsome one.

210
08:22.080 --> 08:25.490
I will finally get to see Gaysorn!

211
08:29.720 --> 08:31.240
Are you serious, Dolly?

212
08:31.450 --> 08:33.539
You mean Dawin has fewer clients

213
08:33.620 --> 08:35.400
because people are turning to AI instead?

214
08:35.640 --> 08:36.600
Will it even be accurate, dear?

215
08:36.730 --> 08:38.400
Do you remember Pha from the film set?

216
08:38.419 --> 08:38.970
Mm.

217
08:39.299 --> 08:41.330
The AI predicted that Pha would be stabbed in the back.

218
08:41.610 --> 08:43.590
They found it as soon as they got home.

219
08:43.610 --> 08:44.390
Their hubby cheated on them?

220
08:44.410 --> 08:45.320
Someone broke into their house!

221
08:46.260 --> 08:47.650
Pha was stabbed in the back.

222
08:47.870 --> 08:48.890
They needed five stitches.

223
08:49.070 --> 08:49.600
Really?

224
08:49.620 --> 08:50.500
Nonsense!

225
08:50.940 --> 08:53.850
How can AI replace humans in the art of spiritual divination?

226
08:53.870 --> 08:54.410
You don't believe me?

227
08:54.840 --> 08:55.610
I'll show you.

228
08:57.280 --> 09:00.490
Can you see if Dawin will have any clients today?

229
09:01.580 --> 09:03.570
Mr. Dawin,

230
09:03.610 --> 09:05.740
your career luck is up and down today.

231
09:05.760 --> 09:08.610
Watch out for meat-related accidents.

232
09:09.650 --> 09:10.690
Isn't it fleet-related?

233
09:10.880 --> 09:11.870
Can't even get the words right.

234
09:12.500 --> 09:13.640
How can it be accurate?

235
09:17.580 --> 09:18.480
If what it said was true...

236
09:18.940 --> 09:20.250
- Oh, hey, hey. - Whoa, whoa.

237
09:20.270 --> 09:21.070
Dolly... Dolly!

238
09:21.090 --> 09:22.830
- Go, go. - Whoa. What, Mom? What?

239
09:22.850 --> 09:23.620
Is he choking?

240
09:23.640 --> 09:24.650
- Is he? - He's choking.

241
09:27.600 --> 09:28.140
Oh!

242
09:28.670 --> 09:30.500
- It really is a meat accident! - Dawin... Dawin!

243
09:30.960 --> 09:31.870
Are you okay?

244
09:31.890 --> 09:32.950
Just you wait,

245
09:32.970 --> 09:34.670
you're finished as a fortune teller, Dawin.

246
09:35.540 --> 09:36.200
Whoa...

247
09:36.220 --> 09:37.470
Then let's see

248
09:37.490 --> 09:39.680
who's more accurate, the AI or me.

249
09:39.700 --> 09:40.240
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

250
09:40.260 --> 09:41.870
- Oh, alright. - Dolly!

251
09:42.100 --> 09:43.050
- Do we have to do this? - Go on.

252
09:43.070 --> 09:44.100
Pick one card.

253
09:44.490 --> 09:45.140
Hurry!

254
09:45.160 --> 09:46.020
Choose wisely, dear.

255
09:48.290 --> 09:50.050
Be careful around high places these days.

256
09:50.380 --> 09:51.730
It could be fatal!

257
09:51.910 --> 09:53.530
Hey, Mom...

258
09:54.800 --> 09:56.490
How high are you talking about? Chair-level?

259
09:56.690 --> 09:57.450
Higher.

260
09:57.470 --> 09:58.200
Chair!

261
09:58.380 --> 09:59.140
Higher!

262
09:59.290 --> 10:00.000
Chair!

263
10:00.020 --> 10:00.700
Even higher!

264
10:00.720 --> 10:01.310
Chair!

265
10:01.330 --> 10:02.120
Even higher!

266
10:02.140 --> 10:03.210
- Chair!! - Higher!!

267
10:03.240 --> 10:05.240
Ugh, dear...

268
10:05.260 --> 10:07.510
Stop messing with him. He's feeling down

269
10:07.530 --> 10:08.620
because he feels insulted by AI.

270
10:08.640 --> 10:09.200
Mm.

271
10:09.220 --> 10:09.910
Just wait and see...

272
10:09.930 --> 10:10.670
Dolly!

273
10:11.530 --> 10:12.200
Hey...

274
10:12.620 --> 10:14.930
you got a medical checkup and hid the results from me, huh?!

275
10:15.360 --> 10:17.380
Dollar, I wasn't hiding it.

276
10:17.400 --> 10:19.660
I just put it somewhere safe

277
10:19.930 --> 10:20.830
so you wouldn't see it.

278
10:20.850 --> 10:21.920
That's called hiding it.

279
10:22.080 --> 10:23.140
And look at these results.

280
10:23.160 --> 10:23.870
Your fat levels are high,

281
10:25.460 --> 10:26.270
your blood sugar is high...

282
10:26.290 --> 10:27.090
Whoa...

283
10:27.850 --> 10:28.670
and your cholesterol is high!

284
10:28.850 --> 10:29.870
See?!

285
10:30.250 --> 10:31.400
You'll die from these high numbers.

286
10:31.420 --> 10:33.150
- Hey, Mom... - Mm.

287
10:33.170 --> 10:34.670
How could you let yourself go this far?

288
10:35.010 --> 10:36.520
Who's gonna help take care of Mom now?

289
10:36.540 --> 10:37.660
Whoa, hey!

290
10:37.680 --> 10:39.020
How can you put all this on me?

291
10:39.220 --> 10:41.320
Tell Mom to take better care of herself, too.

292
10:41.480 --> 10:42.140
Think before you speak.

293
10:42.300 --> 10:43.070
Look at her.

294
10:43.200 --> 10:44.270
She's short,

295
10:44.850 --> 10:45.470
her knees are bad,

296
10:46.420 --> 10:47.280
and her body's sagging.

297
10:47.580 --> 10:48.410
What good would that do?

298
10:48.460 --> 10:50.820
You should be grateful she can still cook and isn't bedridden!

299
10:50.930 --> 10:52.180
- Whoa. - Whoa, there.

300
10:52.200 --> 10:53.520
My dears,

301
10:53.650 --> 10:55.340
if you want to argue, go ahead.

302
10:55.960 --> 10:57.090
But why curse me?

303
10:57.470 --> 10:59.340
- Mom, I'm not cursing you. - Oh?

304
10:59.360 --> 11:00.650
- I just want to push him - Look at him.

305
11:00.680 --> 11:02.570
- to take better care of himself for your sake. - Come on.

306
11:03.840 --> 11:04.670
Go,

307
11:04.820 --> 11:05.500
go get changed.

308
11:05.520 --> 11:06.480
I'm taking you to work out.

309
11:06.500 --> 11:06.880
Go!

310
11:06.900 --> 11:08.090
- Come on. - No!

311
11:08.490 --> 11:10.480
- Come on, go get changed. - I don't wanna be a muscle-obsessed

312
11:10.500 --> 11:12.480
- gym rat like him. - Go get changed...

313
11:12.500 --> 11:13.340
- Oh. - Whoa.

314
11:14.270 --> 11:15.000
- Ow! - Dolly!

315
11:15.030 --> 11:16.200
- Ow! - Dolly.

316
11:16.320 --> 11:17.430
Whoa, Dolly?!

317
11:17.450 --> 11:18.830
Mom... Mom...

318
11:18.850 --> 11:19.710
- Ow! - Dolly!

319
11:19.730 --> 11:20.270
What?

320
11:20.480 --> 11:21.560
- Dolly! - Mom!

321
11:21.580 --> 11:22.840
See? I told you.

322
11:22.860 --> 11:23.870
Be careful around high places.

323
11:23.980 --> 11:25.070
- Yay! - Hey!

324
11:25.480 --> 11:26.630
Now isn't the time for that, is it?

325
11:26.650 --> 11:27.450
My son is hurt.

326
11:27.470 --> 11:28.500
- Go help him. - Mom...

327
11:28.520 --> 11:29.480
- Dolly! - Ow...

328
11:29.500 --> 11:30.040
Dolly!

329
11:30.060 --> 11:31.050
Dolly, Dolly!

330
11:31.070 --> 11:33.010
[The D Dorm]

331
11:33.470 --> 11:34.060
Ugh...

332
11:34.080 --> 11:35.670
- Ow, hey... What? - Oops, sorry.

333
11:35.690 --> 11:36.270
My bad.

334
11:36.290 --> 11:37.580
- Do it properly. - Alright, sorry.

335
11:37.600 --> 11:38.770
Take this seriously...

336
11:38.940 --> 11:40.140
Wait, can I ask you something?

337
11:40.160 --> 11:40.670
Yeah?

338
11:40.800 --> 11:42.820
Why does Grandma have to live in a separate room?

339
11:42.840 --> 11:44.250
Can't she just sleep in her grandson's room?

340
11:44.270 --> 11:46.020
Well, Mr. Dom requested this.

341
11:46.200 --> 11:46.980
Maybe the room

342
11:47.000 --> 11:48.940
is too small for two people.

343
11:50.690 --> 11:51.910
Oh, can I ask you something?

344
11:51.930 --> 11:52.480
Hm?

345
11:52.500 --> 11:54.250
If Grandma moved in,

346
11:54.540 --> 11:55.690
what are we gonna do next?

347
11:55.920 --> 11:57.570
Did Gramps tell you anything in your dreams?

348
11:58.820 --> 12:01.420
Ever since I burned new clothes for him, he hasn't shown his face.

349
12:01.930 --> 12:02.480
Huh?!

350
12:02.500 --> 12:03.730
What do you mean by that?

351
12:05.180 --> 12:05.870
Oh...

352
12:06.040 --> 12:06.880
I mean...

353
12:07.250 --> 12:09.240
He hasn't been visiting me in my dreams at all.

354
12:09.260 --> 12:11.260
- I see... - Yeah.

355
12:14.380 --> 12:17.850
Though we had to go our separate ways,

356
12:17.870 --> 12:21.840
I remember your smile vividly to this day.

357
12:22.560 --> 12:27.660
Though fate and death had parted us,

358
12:27.680 --> 12:31.070
my love for you, my darling...

359
12:32.690 --> 12:34.170
never faded.

360
12:35.730 --> 12:36.460
So?

361
12:36.480 --> 12:37.520
Am I handsome?

362
12:39.280 --> 12:40.700
Has Gaysorn not arrived yet?

363
12:40.720 --> 12:43.820
Everyone, this is the room where Grandma Gaysorn and I

364
12:43.840 --> 12:45.780
will be staying temporarily.

365
12:45.800 --> 12:47.140
Can you say hi to the camera?

366
12:47.160 --> 12:48.930
- Hello, hello. - Hello.

367
12:49.070 --> 12:49.670
Oops...

368
12:49.690 --> 12:51.470
Where is Grandma Gaysorn?

369
12:51.620 --> 12:52.780
She's here with us.

370
12:53.130 --> 12:53.870
Where?

371
13:01.320 --> 13:03.830
Gaysorn!

372
13:10.860 --> 13:11.870
Gaysorn...

373
13:17.500 --> 13:19.050
Dobby, this is not Gaysorn.

374
13:19.070 --> 13:19.860
What?

375
13:21.690 --> 13:22.340
Uh...

376
13:22.360 --> 13:25.660
Are you sure this is Grandma Gaysorn?

377
13:25.680 --> 13:26.840
I sure am.

378
13:27.050 --> 13:29.870
This is the real Grandma Gaysorn,

379
13:29.980 --> 13:32.010
Gramps Danai's first love.

380
13:32.520 --> 13:34.160
Oh...

381
13:34.670 --> 13:36.850
After fifty years apart,

382
13:37.060 --> 13:38.920
Grandma...

383
13:38.940 --> 13:42.280
will finally get to see Gramps in his own home.

384
13:42.620 --> 13:44.090
Gramps Danai,

385
13:44.530 --> 13:47.020
aren't you glad that Grandma finally came home?

386
13:47.040 --> 13:48.260
Glad, my foot!

387
13:48.930 --> 13:50.610
Gaysorn looks nothing like this.

388
13:50.960 --> 13:52.800
Grandma might

389
13:52.820 --> 13:55.320
look a little different because...

390
13:55.650 --> 13:57.470
she was in an accident.

391
13:59.540 --> 14:02.050
Even though Grandma was in an accident,

392
14:02.740 --> 14:06.680
she never forgot about Gramps Danai, not even for a single day.

393
14:06.820 --> 14:08.620
Because she eats [Hawaiian shirt guy, what's his name?]

394
14:08.640 --> 14:10.650
ginkgo candies from the Qilin Pushing Veggie Cart brand. [Grandma is so cute]

395
14:10.670 --> 14:12.920
Nourish your brain and keep Alzheimer's at bay. [What's the surprise today?]

396
14:12.940 --> 14:14.980
Ginkgo candy from the Qilin Pushing [Product details, please]

397
14:15.000 --> 14:15.940
Veggie Cart brand, brand, brand... [Reminds me of my grandma]

398
14:17.360 --> 14:18.180
Ugh.

399
14:18.410 --> 14:20.490
Stop talking about Grandma. Let's get back to the Qilin.

400
14:21.940 --> 14:24.450
Stop talking about the Qilin. Let's get back to Grandma.

401
14:24.470 --> 14:25.400
- Oh... - Mm.

402
14:25.760 --> 14:26.250
Alright.

403
14:26.270 --> 14:27.310
A long time ago...

404
14:27.330 --> 14:27.940
Mm.

405
14:27.960 --> 14:31.310
Grandma missed Gramps terribly.

406
14:31.330 --> 14:35.360
One day, she mistook someone

407
14:35.380 --> 14:36.860
in a passing car for Gramps

408
14:37.200 --> 14:39.790
and ran into the road after him.

409
14:39.810 --> 14:41.700
A durian truck came speeding

410
14:41.720 --> 14:42.910
toward her at 140 kilometers per hour...

411
14:42.930 --> 14:43.960
It crashed into her?

412
14:44.100 --> 14:45.000
She waved it down to buy some.

413
14:45.020 --> 14:45.870
- Oh. - What?

414
14:45.890 --> 14:46.900
But tragically,

415
14:47.290 --> 14:48.500
given the truck's speed,

416
14:48.680 --> 14:50.250
the durians in the back

417
14:50.270 --> 14:53.270
fell straight onto Grandma's face!

418
14:53.520 --> 14:54.680
- Ouch... - Oh...

419
14:54.850 --> 14:57.200
She was paralyzed

420
14:57.600 --> 14:58.530
for the rest of her life.

421
14:58.670 --> 15:00.900
She can no longer move her limbs.

422
15:01.760 --> 15:03.910
Not only that, Grandma

423
15:03.930 --> 15:06.080
had to undergo reconstructive surgery

424
15:06.100 --> 15:08.860
more than ten times to restore her facial structure.

425
15:08.880 --> 15:11.160
That's why she no longer looks anything like she used to.

426
15:11.180 --> 15:13.070
Grandma! Grandma...

427
15:13.180 --> 15:14.820
Why is your life...

428
15:14.840 --> 15:17.570
so tragic, Gaysorn?

429
15:19.490 --> 15:20.270
Poor thing.

430
15:20.520 --> 15:21.040
Hey,

431
15:21.060 --> 15:22.910
isn't being paralyzed after

432
15:22.930 --> 15:25.120
getting hit in the face with a durian a bit far-fetched?

433
15:25.520 --> 15:26.660
It isn't, Ms. Danis.

434
15:27.010 --> 15:28.180
I've heard that

435
15:28.480 --> 15:31.300
a chunk of poop this size once fell from an airplane

436
15:31.410 --> 15:32.510
onto someone's head

437
15:32.530 --> 15:33.450
and nearly killed them.

438
15:33.470 --> 15:34.240
Huh?!

439
15:34.260 --> 15:35.870
Yes, you can't be too careful.

440
15:36.180 --> 15:37.880
The reason I brought her here

441
15:38.010 --> 15:40.060
isn't just to grant her wish,

442
15:40.300 --> 15:41.870
but also to ask for your help.

443
15:42.260 --> 15:43.070
Mr. Dobby.

444
15:43.240 --> 15:43.770
Huh?

445
15:44.140 --> 15:44.940
He wants your help?

446
15:45.170 --> 15:47.280
My family and I had to mortgage our house and land

447
15:47.480 --> 15:49.740
to pay for Grandma's treatment.

448
15:49.760 --> 15:51.950
That's why my Grandma and I...

449
15:51.970 --> 15:53.850
are close to losing the roof over our heads.

450
15:53.870 --> 15:55.070
Oh...

451
15:55.490 --> 15:56.940
Grandma is crying...

452
15:58.570 --> 15:59.940
She's sad...

453
16:01.330 --> 16:01.910
Use this...

454
16:01.930 --> 16:02.650
What are you doing?!

455
16:02.970 --> 16:03.920
I'm going to wipe away her tears.

456
16:04.100 --> 16:04.870
Stop right there.

457
16:04.890 --> 16:07.360
That scratchy tissue is no good for my Grandma's tears.

458
16:08.270 --> 16:09.010
You have to use this.

459
16:09.680 --> 16:10.670
T-REX tissue! [Anyone just got here?]

460
16:10.940 --> 16:13.050
It's thick, tough, and soft. [Could you repeat that? Didn't catch it]

461
16:13.070 --> 16:14.730
Perfect for the delicate skin around your eyes. [He's so good at selling it]

462
16:15.050 --> 16:17.490
T-REX tissue, shoo, shoo, shoo...

463
16:19.580 --> 16:20.420
[Ordered it]

464
16:20.440 --> 16:22.130
Here, let me wipe it for you. [Grandma is so cute]

465
16:22.160 --> 16:22.540
[I ordered it]

466
16:23.520 --> 16:24.480
Is the tissue scratchy, though?

467
16:24.500 --> 16:25.860
I understand that...

468
16:26.270 --> 16:28.070
no one likes it when I do product tie-ins.

469
16:28.520 --> 16:29.240
But...

470
16:29.690 --> 16:30.800
if I don't do this,

471
16:31.530 --> 16:32.770
my grandma and I...

472
16:33.170 --> 16:34.630
won't be able to make ends meet.

473
16:36.260 --> 16:37.440
Dobby...

474
16:37.690 --> 16:39.210
help her.

475
16:40.520 --> 16:41.200
Mr. Dom,

476
16:42.010 --> 16:42.660
how...

477
16:43.290 --> 16:44.530
can I help you?

478
16:47.870 --> 16:48.660
Five million baht.

479
16:48.920 --> 16:49.890
- Huh?! - Huh?!

480
16:50.270 --> 16:51.090
Five million?

481
16:52.540 --> 16:54.150
We need the money to pay off our debts

482
16:54.170 --> 16:55.840
and get our house back.

483
16:55.940 --> 16:56.970
My grandma and I

484
16:57.470 --> 16:58.670
need five million baht.

485
16:59.140 --> 17:00.300
- Five million... - Whoa...

486
17:06.520 --> 17:07.970
Do you feel better now that you have a cast on, dear?

487
17:08.050 --> 17:09.470
I'm okay now, Mom.

488
17:11.540 --> 17:12.900
But I'm not okay.

489
17:13.490 --> 17:14.599
How much longer will you keep this up?

490
17:14.720 --> 17:16.329
You're here, put him down.

491
17:17.020 --> 17:18.099
I can't, Mom.

492
17:18.260 --> 17:20.869
The doctor said, I mustn't let him put

493
17:20.890 --> 17:22.720
any weight on his leg at all, or he'll get hurt.

494
17:22.839 --> 17:25.410
So you let him ride on your back like a dusky langur?

495
17:26.040 --> 17:27.099
Hey, Mom.

496
17:27.119 --> 17:28.060
He deserved it.

497
17:28.180 --> 17:30.260
He's the reason I got hurt.

498
17:30.280 --> 17:31.590
He has to pay!

499
17:31.610 --> 17:32.250
Mm...

500
17:32.270 --> 17:33.020
I want to pee.

501
17:33.040 --> 17:34.720
Take me to the toilet, Khan Kluay.

502
17:36.400 --> 17:37.070
Dolly...

503
17:37.490 --> 17:39.020
Khan Kluay and a dusky langur.

504
17:39.600 --> 17:40.870
Khan Kluay and a dusky langur.

505
17:40.890 --> 17:41.970
Mm, go, go.

506
17:43.730 --> 17:44.640
Here's your ice cream.

507
17:48.010 --> 17:49.680
That ice cream truck took off so fast.

508
17:50.050 --> 17:52.280
Was it trying to win a MotoGP trophy or something?

509
17:53.280 --> 17:54.730
Dollar, are you tired?

510
17:55.960 --> 17:57.690
Can you go grab my charger for me?

511
17:59.120 --> 18:00.460
It's alright, I'll go get it myself.

512
18:00.480 --> 18:01.350
Just sit there.

513
18:01.370 --> 18:02.270
I'll get it for you.

514
18:02.620 --> 18:03.290
Your charger, right?

515
18:04.670 --> 18:05.380
Here...

516
18:06.130 --> 18:07.050
Okay, one sec.

517
18:07.070 --> 18:08.080
Ow...

518
18:12.460 --> 18:13.070
Anything else?

519
18:16.220 --> 18:17.010
I'll teach him a lesson.

520
18:20.270 --> 18:21.120
Is that all?

521
18:29.680 --> 18:31.070
Here's your shrimp fried rice.

522
18:31.890 --> 18:33.450
Wait, wait, wait, Dolly,

523
18:33.470 --> 18:35.220
I can make you shrimp fried rice.

524
18:35.240 --> 18:37.070
Why did you make him buy it from somewhere else?

525
18:37.300 --> 18:38.480
Well, I'm bored of it.

526
18:38.680 --> 18:41.040
I wanted to switch things up a little.

527
18:41.460 --> 18:42.820
You're messing with your brother,

528
18:43.370 --> 18:44.760
aren't you?

529
18:45.640 --> 18:48.500
And you, you're spoiling him too much.

530
18:48.520 --> 18:49.700
It was my fault,

531
18:49.810 --> 18:51.160
so I have to take responsibility.

532
18:51.180 --> 18:52.490
So I won't owe him anything.

533
18:53.490 --> 18:54.440
I've taken time off work.

534
18:54.780 --> 18:56.940
From now on, I'll be your legs

535
18:57.660 --> 18:58.670
until you recover.

536
19:00.610 --> 19:02.270
Okay, Dollar.

537
19:03.610 --> 19:04.740
Who's calling me?

538
19:05.520 --> 19:06.400
Yes, Oeng?

539
19:07.930 --> 19:08.520
Oh,

540
19:08.960 --> 19:10.180
the cafe at the entrance of the alley?

541
19:10.200 --> 19:10.810
I'll go.

542
19:11.160 --> 19:12.260
I've never been there before.

543
19:12.730 --> 19:13.350
Yeah, yeah.

544
19:13.370 --> 19:14.510
- Hey, hey... - Oh, oh?

545
19:14.530 --> 19:15.320
Hey, what are you doing?

546
19:15.600 --> 19:17.100
You're going to the cafe, aren't you?

547
19:17.120 --> 19:18.680
- No need. - I already told you I'd be your legs.

548
19:18.700 --> 19:19.050
Come on.

549
19:19.070 --> 19:20.670
Hey, wait. Don't, don't.

550
19:20.690 --> 19:22.280
It's embarrassing. There are too many people.

551
19:22.300 --> 19:23.380
My friends are there.

552
19:23.650 --> 19:25.050
Mom, tell him to stop.

553
19:25.070 --> 19:25.750
Mom...

554
19:25.770 --> 19:27.450
He's your legs, not mine.

555
19:27.470 --> 19:28.650
Tell him yourself.

556
19:28.670 --> 19:30.210
Mom!

557
19:35.910 --> 19:39.210
[The D Dorm]

558
19:42.520 --> 19:43.390
Ugh!

559
19:43.410 --> 19:44.890
There goes my image.

560
19:45.300 --> 19:46.410
Dollar was carrying me around

561
19:46.670 --> 19:48.670
like I was his pocket dog.

562
19:48.690 --> 19:50.270
I'm starting to regret this.

563
19:50.400 --> 19:51.980
I shouldn't have faked my injury.

564
19:52.240 --> 19:52.960
What?

565
19:53.410 --> 19:54.440
So it was all an act?

566
19:55.970 --> 19:56.940
You were faking your injury

567
19:56.960 --> 19:59.370
because you didn't want to be forced to exercise?

568
20:01.770 --> 20:02.690
- Ugh! - Whoa?!

569
20:02.900 --> 20:03.940
Why are you angry?

570
20:04.050 --> 20:04.980
I'm angry at myself

571
20:05.330 --> 20:06.660
for losing to AI.

572
20:06.680 --> 20:09.130
I really thought you were injured after falling from a high place.

573
20:09.580 --> 20:10.300
Hey,

574
20:10.960 --> 20:13.130
you have to keep this a secret.

575
20:13.330 --> 20:15.020
Don't tell Dollar about this.

576
20:15.040 --> 20:16.140
- Dang it! - Whoa!

577
20:16.160 --> 20:17.640
What?! Why are you angry again?!

578
20:17.660 --> 20:18.730
I'm angry at myself again.

579
20:18.850 --> 20:20.270
If I lost to AI...

580
20:20.620 --> 20:22.130
how am I supposed to make money?!

581
20:22.260 --> 20:24.840
Stop obsessing over AI and start caring about other people.

582
20:28.340 --> 20:29.370
Yes, Pha?

583
20:29.960 --> 20:32.360
An ad shoot needs a stylist urgently for tomorrow?

584
20:32.890 --> 20:34.260
Double pay?!

585
20:34.280 --> 20:35.850
Oh, of course I can go.

586
20:35.870 --> 20:38.330
I'm free tomorrow, so I'll go.

587
20:39.680 --> 20:40.490
Where are you going?

588
20:41.980 --> 20:42.920
How did you get here?

589
20:42.940 --> 20:44.270
Well, I'm your legs.

590
20:44.520 --> 20:46.170
Wherever you go, I go.

591
20:46.290 --> 20:47.960
By the way, you're working tomorrow?

592
20:47.980 --> 20:48.790
How are you gonna get there?

593
20:48.810 --> 20:49.720
I can go.

594
20:50.100 --> 20:51.280
I asked Drip for help.

595
20:51.300 --> 20:52.840
He'll take care of me on set.

596
20:53.020 --> 20:53.870
Not just Drip.

597
20:54.580 --> 20:56.270
I'll help him out as well.

598
20:56.410 --> 20:56.930
Huh?!

599
20:58.220 --> 20:59.300
If you try to stop me,

600
20:59.760 --> 21:01.050
I'm gonna expose you.

601
21:01.070 --> 21:02.270
Oh, so that's how you're gonna do it, huh?

602
21:02.640 --> 21:03.470
Mm, yes.

603
21:03.600 --> 21:04.670
You don't need to go.

604
21:04.780 --> 21:06.040
I already have a lot of people looking after me.

605
21:06.060 --> 21:06.650
No!

606
21:06.810 --> 21:08.010
I said I'm your legs,

607
21:08.410 --> 21:09.970
so I'm going, too.

608
21:12.760 --> 21:13.760
How sweet...

609
21:13.780 --> 21:15.290
I want to cut my leg off.

610
21:16.180 --> 21:17.360
I want to cut my leg off...

611
21:21.250 --> 21:24.230
Are you really gonna pay him five million baht?

612
21:26.880 --> 21:28.430
If Gramps were still alive,

613
21:28.530 --> 21:30.500
he'd definitely help Grandma Gaysorn.

614
21:31.180 --> 21:32.270
What are you gonna do?

615
21:34.140 --> 21:34.920
I'm not paying him.

616
21:36.120 --> 21:37.920
Not until I see all of the medical bills.

617
21:39.520 --> 21:40.460
That way, I can be sure that

618
21:41.240 --> 21:42.720
he isn't trying to scam us.

619
21:48.700 --> 21:54.100
I want to repent of my sins.

620
21:54.120 --> 21:59.210
I want to be punched in the chin, one, two, three.

621
21:59.760 --> 22:04.670
If I could turn back time, I would be your guard

622
22:05.580 --> 22:10.480
and protect you, ooh-ooh.

623
22:10.500 --> 22:13.360
Ooh-ooh, ooh-ooh.

624
22:13.380 --> 22:14.060
Bam!

625
22:14.080 --> 22:14.520
Bam!

626
22:15.250 --> 22:16.210
What are you looking at?

627
22:16.330 --> 22:17.210
I am drunk, you see?

628
22:18.090 --> 22:18.920
Mr. Dobby,

629
22:19.770 --> 22:20.770
be real with me,

630
22:21.020 --> 22:22.450
do you even have five million baht?

631
22:23.120 --> 22:26.020
You might have to sell this dorm to pay him.

632
22:26.840 --> 22:29.500
But this dorm is Gramps' beloved place, too.

633
22:30.410 --> 22:32.480
You're not gonna sell it just to pay them, right?

634
22:34.520 --> 22:35.680
I'm not going to sell it.

635
22:35.700 --> 22:36.900
I told you I'm not selling it.

636
22:37.070 --> 22:38.270
So I won't sell it.

637
22:38.450 --> 22:39.470
Liar!

638
22:40.560 --> 22:41.340
I am drunk,

639
22:41.360 --> 22:42.470
so I want to listen to the lyre.

640
22:42.490 --> 22:44.130
I was not insulting you.

641
22:45.170 --> 22:46.440
- Mr. Dobby. - Hm?

642
22:46.460 --> 22:48.740
Mr. Dom is livestreaming with his grandma again.

643
22:48.760 --> 22:49.680
What? Let me see.

644
22:49.810 --> 22:51.000
Grandma,

645
22:51.020 --> 22:52.280
this is our Gramps Danai.

646
22:53.320 --> 22:54.490
Oh, Grandma...

647
22:54.660 --> 22:57.280
It'd be nice if you got to meet him

648
22:57.300 --> 22:58.140
while he was still alive.

649
22:58.410 --> 23:00.720
He would've definitely helped you,

650
23:01.070 --> 23:03.890
unlike his grandson, who's still hesitating, right?

651
23:06.570 --> 23:07.690
Dobby!

652
23:08.080 --> 23:09.680
You have to help Gaysorn.

653
23:09.700 --> 23:12.540
I do not want to be any more wrong than I already am!

654
23:13.520 --> 23:14.740
Look at me.

655
23:14.940 --> 23:17.360
Why aren't you talking to me, Dobby?!

656
23:17.380 --> 23:18.610
Huh?!

657
23:21.100 --> 23:22.670
What a ridiculous ghost.

658
23:22.930 --> 23:24.250
I shouldn't have given him alcohol.

659
23:25.520 --> 23:26.550
It's alright,

660
23:26.800 --> 23:28.670
I'll protect you.

661
23:29.870 --> 23:30.840
Whoa, whoa.

662
23:31.070 --> 23:32.830
Just like this Furious Betta Mosquito Repellent Cream,

663
23:32.850 --> 23:34.380
you betta use it if you don't want to get bitten.

664
23:34.400 --> 23:36.240
Don't forget to buy this for yourself.

665
23:36.370 --> 23:37.480
He used to get fewer than a thousand viewers.

666
23:37.500 --> 23:40.670
Since her incident, his views have hit tens of thousands.

667
23:41.720 --> 23:42.550
It's only natural.

668
23:42.570 --> 23:45.450
People are more interested in other people's business than their own.

669
23:45.470 --> 23:46.760
It's normal.

670
23:48.610 --> 23:49.990
Yes, we're at...

671
23:50.010 --> 23:52.290
the D Dorm where my grandma...

672
23:53.660 --> 23:54.890
Gaysorn...

673
23:55.370 --> 23:58.050
I'm right here, Gaysorn...

674
23:59.360 --> 24:01.980
Seeing you

675
24:02.490 --> 24:04.940
feels like meeting the one

676
24:05.330 --> 24:09.000
I have always yearned for.

677
24:09.240 --> 24:11.870
You are the woman of my dreams.

678
24:13.410 --> 24:16.860
I am such a genius at this.

679
24:16.880 --> 24:18.490
If I became a lyricist,

680
24:18.920 --> 24:20.780
I would shoot to fame.

681
24:21.740 --> 24:23.060
What a ridiculous ghost.

682
24:24.480 --> 24:25.070
Mr. Dom,

683
24:25.760 --> 24:26.760
may I have a moment?

684
24:27.180 --> 24:28.820
I'm still livestreaming, though.

685
24:28.840 --> 24:31.170
You wouldn't mind if we talk while I livestream, right?

686
24:31.200 --> 24:31.900
Oh...

687
24:31.920 --> 24:32.800
- Alright. - Say hello to the camera.

688
24:32.940 --> 24:34.060
- Uh, hello. - Yes.

689
24:34.360 --> 24:35.170
Um...

690
24:35.640 --> 24:37.520
Grandma Gaysorn had surgery, right?

691
24:37.980 --> 24:39.840
Could I see the medical bills?

692
24:40.150 --> 24:41.610
You think I'm scamming you, don't you?

693
24:42.740 --> 24:44.840
I don't have those medical bills.

694
24:45.970 --> 24:47.870
Because I'm not here to ask you for money.

695
24:48.660 --> 24:50.270
All I ask for is your empathy.

696
24:51.470 --> 24:53.210
My grandma is in this state

697
24:53.600 --> 24:54.920
partly because your grandpa

698
24:56.270 --> 24:57.450
broke his promise

699
24:57.470 --> 24:59.340
and refused to run away with her to Chiang Mai.

700
25:00.900 --> 25:01.870
Whoa...

701
25:01.890 --> 25:02.470
Ms. Danis,

702
25:02.490 --> 25:03.740
the people are against us.

703
25:03.760 --> 25:05.280
They're threatening to boycott our dorm, too.

704
25:05.440 --> 25:06.130
What?

705
25:06.500 --> 25:07.190
Hey...

706
25:07.210 --> 25:09.730
He says we can take this to Judge Jammy.

707
25:12.520 --> 25:13.070
Hey,

708
25:13.260 --> 25:14.060
listen!

709
25:14.080 --> 25:16.650
Mr. Dobby isn't asking you because he doesn't want to pay you.

710
25:16.670 --> 25:19.050
Five million baht is a lot.

711
25:19.070 --> 25:20.940
He wants proof.

712
25:21.300 --> 25:22.960
Proof that you paid, you know?

713
25:22.980 --> 25:24.210
If you don't have that with you,

714
25:24.560 --> 25:26.270
you can tell us the name of the hospital you went to.

715
25:26.520 --> 25:28.050
We can try to figure it out ourselves.

716
25:28.170 --> 25:28.670
Yes...

717
25:28.960 --> 25:30.570
If you don't want to help, that's okay.

718
25:31.070 --> 25:32.810
I'll take Grandma back to Chiang Mai.

719
25:33.050 --> 25:35.480
She was abandoned by Grandpa once before.

720
25:36.020 --> 25:37.370
I guess being abandoned again

721
25:38.050 --> 25:39.010
wouldn't make much difference.

722
25:45.340 --> 25:46.120
Dobby.

723
25:46.380 --> 25:47.520
Gaysorn...

724
25:47.860 --> 25:48.830
She swatted a mosquito!

725
25:48.850 --> 25:50.250
She was moving.

726
25:50.270 --> 25:52.650
She is no longer paralyzed.

727
25:52.670 --> 25:55.070
She is not paralyzed anymore!

728
26:01.730 --> 26:02.480
Mr. Dom,

729
26:03.930 --> 26:05.130
you want five million baht, right?

730
26:05.660 --> 26:06.160
Yes.

731
26:06.180 --> 26:07.070
I'll pay you tomorrow.

732
26:07.260 --> 26:07.820
Huh?!

733
26:09.640 --> 26:10.980
Thank you so much

734
26:11.000 --> 26:13.450
for understanding our struggle.

735
26:13.480 --> 26:16.160
Just like Seal Life Insurance understands Thai people's struggles.

736
26:16.180 --> 26:17.870
Insurance made easy.

737
26:18.000 --> 26:19.720
Let this be your safety net.

738
26:19.960 --> 26:22.650
Ung, ung, ung, ung, ung, ung...

739
26:25.010 --> 26:27.270
[The D Dorm]

740
26:30.320 --> 26:31.130
Whoa?!

741
26:31.630 --> 26:32.960
It's just like you said.

742
26:32.980 --> 26:33.970
They're lying to us.

743
26:33.990 --> 26:35.510
Ugh, these con artists.

744
26:35.690 --> 26:37.710
I'll curse them till they run to jail!

745
26:37.730 --> 26:38.590
- Hey, hey, calm down. - Whoa.

746
26:38.610 --> 26:39.850
Ms. Danis, come back.

747
26:39.870 --> 26:40.660
What now?

748
26:40.680 --> 26:42.210
Take a sniff. It'll calm you down.

749
26:42.660 --> 26:43.080
Huh?

750
26:43.380 --> 26:45.010
An inhaler from Chicken Ben Dover.

751
26:45.310 --> 26:47.420
Justin Hale, you'll like it.

752
26:48.050 --> 26:49.060
Ugh!

753
26:49.080 --> 26:51.210
Copying Dom will only make me angrier.

754
26:51.870 --> 26:52.520
Give it to me!

755
26:52.540 --> 26:54.270
What were you thinking, messing with an angry person?

756
26:54.420 --> 26:55.450
We don't know

757
26:56.200 --> 26:58.220
what else they lied about,

758
26:58.420 --> 27:02.300
but the fact that he has something Grandpa gave to Grandma Gaysorn

759
27:02.850 --> 27:04.060
means that...

760
27:04.680 --> 27:06.490
they probably know Grandma Gaysorn.

761
27:06.930 --> 27:09.100
We have to get more information from them.

762
27:11.030 --> 27:12.250
What a bright idea.

763
27:13.310 --> 27:15.050
If we let Ms. Danis complain to them,

764
27:15.070 --> 27:16.660
she'll throw a whip in the works.

765
27:16.680 --> 27:17.470
- Huh?! - Huh?!

766
27:17.580 --> 27:18.640
Throw a wronch in the wake.

767
27:18.660 --> 27:19.290
- Huh?! - Huh?!

768
27:19.310 --> 27:20.390
Throw a wrench in the wuss.

769
27:20.410 --> 27:21.130
- Huh?! - Huh?!

770
27:21.260 --> 27:22.660
Whatever I'm trying to throw, it's not your concern.

771
27:22.680 --> 27:23.250
Ugh.

772
27:23.880 --> 27:24.820
Dobby,

773
27:25.550 --> 27:26.960
do not accuse her of those things yet.

774
27:26.980 --> 27:30.090
She might actually be Gaysorn.

775
27:30.110 --> 27:31.310
Perhaps...

776
27:31.610 --> 27:35.860
my poem stirred her neurons,

777
27:35.880 --> 27:40.510
so her body miraculously recovered from paralysis.

778
27:41.610 --> 27:42.530
Mr. Dobby,

779
27:42.590 --> 27:45.110
how are we going to

780
27:45.480 --> 27:47.370
get information from them, though?

781
27:48.660 --> 27:49.510
Yeah...

782
27:50.070 --> 27:51.130
True.

783
27:51.480 --> 27:52.490
I have a plan.

784
27:53.880 --> 27:54.870
What plan?

785
28:00.020 --> 28:00.810
We're going to

786
28:01.870 --> 28:04.410
tear the masks off those two tomorrow.

787
28:17.040 --> 28:17.730
Mr. Drip.

788
28:18.170 --> 28:18.490
Yes?

789
28:18.510 --> 28:21.050
Can you grab the blood-red shirt for me?

790
28:21.070 --> 28:21.480
Yes.

791
28:23.250 --> 28:24.480
Blood-red...

792
28:25.250 --> 28:25.820
So...

793
28:25.980 --> 28:27.240
what exactly is the color of blood?

794
28:28.680 --> 28:30.910
Is it the same as the blood in the noodles we eat?

795
28:31.080 --> 28:32.880
I don't know how to explain it either.

796
28:33.210 --> 28:33.890
It's alright.

797
28:34.030 --> 28:34.730
I'll grab it myself.

798
28:35.230 --> 28:35.880
Stop right there.

799
28:36.190 --> 28:37.080
Let me do it for you.

800
28:42.060 --> 28:42.490
Mm.

801
28:42.830 --> 28:43.510
It's this one, right?

802
28:50.850 --> 28:52.680
Mr. Drip, can you give me my water bottle?

803
28:52.790 --> 28:53.300
Okay.

804
28:53.530 --> 28:54.260
I'll grab it for you.

805
28:56.530 --> 28:57.270
Here.

806
29:03.990 --> 29:05.080
Alright, fetch.

807
29:05.330 --> 29:06.230
Right away.

808
29:06.720 --> 29:07.530
Hey!

809
29:07.820 --> 29:09.180
This isn't funny.

810
29:10.140 --> 29:12.290
I'm not trying to be funny.

811
29:12.590 --> 29:14.480
My leg just hurts. I'm still fine.

812
29:14.770 --> 29:15.940
Why did you have to follow me here?

813
29:16.140 --> 29:16.970
Just go home.

814
29:16.990 --> 29:17.880
No.

815
29:18.410 --> 29:21.170
Mom already lost Dad. She can't lose you, too.

816
29:21.750 --> 29:22.520
For Mom's sake,

817
29:22.540 --> 29:25.270
I won't let anything happen to you again.

818
29:25.990 --> 29:27.260
Ugh...

819
29:27.350 --> 29:28.230
All done?

820
29:28.250 --> 29:29.170
Yes.

821
29:30.030 --> 29:31.400
It's uncomfortable.

822
29:36.890 --> 29:39.120
Accept the truth, then.

823
29:39.520 --> 29:40.570
Never.

824
29:46.430 --> 29:48.650
Ugh, it's so itchy...

825
29:50.070 --> 29:51.230
What should I do?

826
29:51.250 --> 29:52.680
I can't take my cast off here, either.

827
29:53.700 --> 29:54.750
Are you alright?

828
29:56.930 --> 29:57.810
What's wrong?

829
29:57.830 --> 29:58.780
What should I do?

830
29:59.700 --> 30:00.490
Dollar!

831
30:00.790 --> 30:02.060
I'm going to the toilet.

832
30:02.280 --> 30:02.830
Whoa, whoa.

833
30:03.070 --> 30:03.990
Get on my back.

834
30:05.230 --> 30:05.640
What?

835
30:05.660 --> 30:06.310
Come on.

836
30:08.830 --> 30:09.320
What?

837
30:09.340 --> 30:10.300
Why are you heavier than usual?

838
30:10.680 --> 30:12.510
Oh, it's probably because of the cast.

839
30:15.020 --> 30:15.480
Oh.

840
30:15.710 --> 30:16.190
Ugh!

841
30:16.350 --> 30:16.950
Ugh...

842
30:17.090 --> 30:17.510
Oh.

843
30:17.650 --> 30:18.370
I can't take this anymore.

844
30:19.540 --> 30:20.280
Ugh!

845
30:21.140 --> 30:21.850
Here

846
30:22.150 --> 30:23.150
is your check for five million baht.

847
30:23.780 --> 30:26.420
Hey, it's five million. Are you sure this is alright?

848
30:26.610 --> 30:28.260
I already agreed to this.

849
30:32.220 --> 30:33.550
Thank you so much, Mr. Dobby.

850
30:33.610 --> 30:34.380
Wait.

851
30:34.530 --> 30:35.530
I'll definitely give it to you,

852
30:36.450 --> 30:37.590
but there's one condition.

853
30:37.630 --> 30:38.530
Condition...?

854
30:39.010 --> 30:40.900
Last night, Grandpa came into my dream.

855
30:41.150 --> 30:42.250
He wanted me

856
30:42.440 --> 30:43.790
to help treat Grandma Gaysorn

857
30:43.810 --> 30:46.090
so that she could walk again.

858
30:48.370 --> 30:50.280
But her doctor said that

859
30:50.620 --> 30:52.660
she won't be able to walk anymore, though.

860
30:52.680 --> 30:54.170
Mr. Dom, you have to understand that

861
30:54.420 --> 30:55.450
those doctors are quacks.

862
30:55.830 --> 30:56.260
Huh?

863
30:56.280 --> 30:57.690
But the person I brought today

864
30:57.710 --> 30:59.250
is a miracle doctor.

865
30:59.590 --> 31:00.170
Huh?!

866
31:00.570 --> 31:01.560
Doctor Chen!

867
31:14.280 --> 31:15.160
- Hello, Doctor Chen. - Hello.

868
31:15.180 --> 31:16.000
Hello.

869
31:16.020 --> 31:17.860
- Hello, Doctor Chen. - Mm, hello.

870
31:17.880 --> 31:18.760
Would you like me to help?

871
31:18.780 --> 31:19.950
It is alright.

872
31:20.860 --> 31:21.710
This is

873
31:21.980 --> 31:22.680
Doctor Chen.

874
31:23.030 --> 31:25.910
He's an expert at treating paralysis.

875
31:26.070 --> 31:28.140
He just came down from a mountain.

876
31:28.270 --> 31:29.330
Lingshan Mountain?

877
31:29.350 --> 31:30.010
The Golden Mount.

878
31:30.930 --> 31:33.290
He's here to rent a balloon-dart booth for this year's Loy Krathong.

879
31:33.660 --> 31:34.680
So it was the perfect opportunity

880
31:34.700 --> 31:36.210
to ask him for help.

881
31:36.910 --> 31:37.890
Doctor Chen,

882
31:38.280 --> 31:40.200
do you think Grandma Gaysorn

883
31:40.220 --> 31:41.100
can be treated?

884
31:41.290 --> 31:44.130
I will have to checker reflexes.

885
31:44.150 --> 31:45.650
Why checkers, though?

886
31:45.670 --> 31:46.660
Checker reflexes.

887
31:46.680 --> 31:48.680
Now is not the time for checkers. Treat her first.

888
31:48.700 --> 31:50.260
Check-er reflexes.

889
31:50.280 --> 31:51.880
- Check her reflexes! - Mm.

890
31:51.900 --> 31:53.880
Oh, let me find my things...

891
31:54.710 --> 31:55.490
Here.

892
31:55.630 --> 31:56.280
- Whoa. - Whoa!

893
31:56.550 --> 31:58.100
Too small, too small.

894
31:59.880 --> 32:00.880
- Whoa?! - Huh?!

895
32:00.900 --> 32:01.750
Mm.

896
32:01.770 --> 32:02.830
Still too small.

897
32:02.850 --> 32:03.280
Whoa...

898
32:03.300 --> 32:04.680
- Still too small. - Too small?

899
32:05.740 --> 32:07.060
- Oh, whoa! - Huh?!

900
32:07.080 --> 32:07.540
Mm.

901
32:07.700 --> 32:09.590
This is perfect.

902
32:09.610 --> 32:11.860
- It fits perfectly in my hand. - Wow.

903
32:11.880 --> 32:12.570
Dobby,

904
32:12.590 --> 32:14.030
are you really going to do this?!

905
32:14.610 --> 32:16.680
Gaysorn, I cannot bear to keep looking at this.

906
32:16.930 --> 32:17.880
I am leaving.

907
32:18.850 --> 32:20.130
Wait, stop.

908
32:20.280 --> 32:21.460
What are you going to do to my grandma?

909
32:21.480 --> 32:22.680
I will examine her.

910
32:23.710 --> 32:24.530
Mr. Dom,

911
32:24.950 --> 32:26.980
if you want that five million,

912
32:27.220 --> 32:28.970
you'll have to let Doctor Chen

913
32:29.000 --> 32:30.750
examine her.

914
32:30.860 --> 32:31.990
But don't worry,

915
32:32.140 --> 32:34.370
Dr. Chen is highly skilled.

916
32:34.630 --> 32:36.610
- He won't make any mistakes. - Mm, do not worry.

917
32:36.630 --> 32:37.500
Be careful.

918
32:41.180 --> 32:42.310
Ow!

919
32:42.330 --> 32:43.860
Ow...

920
32:44.650 --> 32:45.790
I shouldn't have stood there...

921
32:45.810 --> 32:46.530
Handyman Daeng.

922
32:46.630 --> 32:49.210
That was an example

923
32:49.230 --> 32:51.790
to show you what a normal reflex is like.

924
32:51.810 --> 32:53.510
- Oh, a demonstration. - I see.

925
32:54.010 --> 32:54.500
Alright, alright.

926
32:54.740 --> 32:56.740
Now it is your turn, Grandma.

927
32:56.940 --> 32:57.480
Oh...

928
32:58.030 --> 32:58.680
Mm.

929
33:00.610 --> 33:03.170
Her nerves might not have been stimulated for a long time.

930
33:03.190 --> 33:05.660
I have to wake them up.

931
33:25.260 --> 33:25.990
- What?! - Whoa, whoa!

932
33:26.010 --> 33:28.390
Grandma lifted her leg! I saw it with my own eyes!

933
33:28.540 --> 33:29.060
Well...

934
33:29.180 --> 33:29.880
I was kicked.

935
33:30.050 --> 33:31.450
What a miracle.

936
33:32.130 --> 33:33.820
Grandma can finally move her leg again.

937
33:34.230 --> 33:36.550
Thank you so much, Doc, for treating my grandma.

938
33:36.570 --> 33:38.620
But I'll take care of her after this.

939
33:38.940 --> 33:39.480
Thank you.

940
33:40.250 --> 33:40.940
Wait!

941
33:41.710 --> 33:43.500
Why are you in such a rush?

942
33:43.890 --> 33:47.530
Doctor Chen's treatment isn't even done yet.

943
33:51.850 --> 33:52.480
I was kicked.

944
33:52.500 --> 33:54.260
Right in my face.

945
33:55.620 --> 33:58.970
Her nerves still work,

946
33:59.100 --> 34:01.080
but they need to be stimulated.

947
34:01.290 --> 34:02.850
Next,

948
34:02.870 --> 34:05.370
I will have her steamed with herbs

949
34:05.530 --> 34:07.690
to boost her circulation.

950
34:07.710 --> 34:08.540
Come, come.

951
34:09.030 --> 34:11.659
It's just herbal steam. Nothing to worry about, right?

952
34:12.659 --> 34:13.489
Just a little longer, okay?

953
34:13.510 --> 34:15.850
But herbs may not be enough.

954
34:15.870 --> 34:18.520
We need some toksin.

955
34:18.540 --> 34:19.679
Oh, what should we talk about?

956
34:19.699 --> 34:20.449
Toksin.

957
34:20.469 --> 34:21.460
You're gonna do it now, right?

958
34:21.480 --> 34:22.370
Tok-sin.

959
34:22.550 --> 34:23.370
Oh, toxins!

960
34:23.389 --> 34:23.880
- Mm. - Oh.

961
34:24.050 --> 34:24.949
- Whoa... - Toxins.

962
34:24.969 --> 34:27.370
Handyman Daeng, are you ready?

963
34:27.400 --> 34:29.389
- Whoa! - Whoa!

964
34:29.409 --> 34:31.080
- So scary. - Oh, wow...

965
34:31.300 --> 34:33.480
Start with scorpions.

966
34:34.860 --> 34:38.060
Handyman Daeng, be careful. They're huge.

967
34:38.510 --> 34:40.179
Then add in the toads.

968
34:40.330 --> 34:41.730
- Whoa, how many are there? - Oh, wow!

969
34:41.750 --> 34:43.060
- Get it there. - Pour them in.

970
34:43.080 --> 34:44.980
Put them all in there.

971
34:45.300 --> 34:46.920
Next, add in the centipedes.

972
34:46.940 --> 34:48.130
Add in the centipedes.

973
34:49.659 --> 34:51.650
- Put them all in there. - Hey...

974
34:51.670 --> 34:52.530
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

975
34:52.550 --> 34:54.330
What are you trying to do to her?

976
34:54.350 --> 34:57.300
Are you treating my grandma or turning her into a poison monster?

977
34:57.350 --> 34:58.470
If my grandma goes in there,

978
34:58.490 --> 34:59.200
she's gonna die.

979
34:59.220 --> 35:01.400
This is not fatal. It is just mild venom.

980
35:01.420 --> 35:03.210
- Mild venom. - No need to worry.

981
35:03.230 --> 35:04.680
So, are you done?

982
35:04.860 --> 35:05.880
Huh?!

983
35:06.470 --> 35:07.530
I dropped the container!

984
35:07.670 --> 35:09.460
Oh no, you dropped it.

985
35:09.480 --> 35:10.240
Uh...

986
35:10.260 --> 35:11.010
I'll...

987
35:11.230 --> 35:12.150
use my hand...

988
35:12.510 --> 35:13.390
to pick it up.

989
35:13.620 --> 35:15.900
Are you sure that's a good idea? Don't risk it.

990
35:21.100 --> 35:23.600
Ow, ow, ow!

991
35:24.630 --> 35:25.410
Handyman Daeng.

992
35:25.430 --> 35:26.710
Ow!

993
35:28.490 --> 35:30.300
Hey, what's wrong?!

994
35:31.310 --> 35:31.840
What?!

995
35:31.860 --> 35:33.950
He's foaming at the mouth.

996
35:33.970 --> 35:34.890
Handyman Daeng,

997
35:35.230 --> 35:37.060
you left us far too soon.

998
35:37.080 --> 35:38.360
Oh...

999
35:38.580 --> 35:41.020
It is normal for accidents to happen.

1000
35:41.290 --> 35:42.790
They do not happen very often, anyway.

1001
35:42.810 --> 35:43.700
Dobby.

1002
35:43.720 --> 35:45.280
- Huh? - Bring her in here.

1003
35:46.260 --> 35:46.680
Grandma.

1004
35:46.700 --> 35:47.980
- Mm. - She'll finally be able to walk.

1005
35:48.010 --> 35:48.850
Excuse me, Mr. Dom.

1006
35:55.890 --> 35:56.280
What?

1007
35:56.470 --> 35:57.920
- Whoa! - Oh, wow!

1008
35:57.940 --> 36:00.310
We've just started, but Grandma has already regained her strength.

1009
36:01.730 --> 36:02.950
- Splendid. - You can do this, Grandma.

1010
36:02.970 --> 36:04.100
How miraculous.

1011
36:04.500 --> 36:05.880
The treatment worked so well.

1012
36:07.790 --> 36:08.490
Let's go!

1013
36:10.110 --> 36:11.310
I give up!

1014
36:11.330 --> 36:13.480
Stop! No more of this!

1015
36:13.500 --> 36:14.500
Dom,

1016
36:14.620 --> 36:15.480
you get in there yourself!

1017
36:15.740 --> 36:17.540
I'm not doing this! I'm leaving!

1018
36:18.230 --> 36:19.330
Stop right there.

1019
36:19.350 --> 36:20.770
Where do you think you're going?

1020
36:21.010 --> 36:25.510
You're all better now, Grandma Gaysorn?

1021
36:25.530 --> 36:26.890
Dearie...

1022
36:28.230 --> 36:30.530
I'm not Grandma Gaysorn.

1023
36:31.690 --> 36:34.420
Dom brought me here.

1024
36:37.710 --> 36:38.280
Uh...

1025
36:39.530 --> 36:40.540
Huh?!

1026
36:40.680 --> 36:42.330
You're not Grandma Gaysorn?

1027
36:42.500 --> 36:43.730
Your name isn't Gaysorn?

1028
36:43.750 --> 36:46.370
You've been lying to me my whole life?

1029
36:46.930 --> 36:48.050
I'm sad.

1030
36:48.070 --> 36:49.530
I'm so sad.

1031
36:49.860 --> 36:51.330
Then...

1032
36:51.350 --> 36:53.210
let me go home and cry.

1033
36:53.880 --> 36:55.190
- Hey! - Mr. Dom,

1034
36:55.210 --> 36:56.540
you can cry in there.

1035
36:57.350 --> 36:58.680
Get in there.

1036
37:00.450 --> 37:01.080
Huh?

1037
37:01.750 --> 37:02.910
So?

1038
37:06.140 --> 37:07.340
- They're fake? - Mm.

1039
37:10.060 --> 37:11.300
Did you trick me?

1040
37:11.440 --> 37:13.060
We simply gave you a taste of your own medicine.

1041
37:13.080 --> 37:13.790
That's right!

1042
37:13.930 --> 37:15.780
You fake grandson.

1043
37:21.300 --> 37:23.140
Ugh...

1044
37:23.600 --> 37:25.070
There are rashes everywhere.

1045
37:25.580 --> 37:27.460
Dolly!

1046
37:27.480 --> 37:28.490
- Ow! - Ow!

1047
37:28.820 --> 37:29.860
- Ow! - Ow, ow.

1048
37:29.880 --> 37:31.370
Ugh, Dawin!

1049
37:31.390 --> 37:32.340
What were you running from?

1050
37:32.430 --> 37:34.220
I read the assistant director's fortune.

1051
37:34.390 --> 37:36.500
They challenged me to see who was more accurate, the AI or me.

1052
37:36.670 --> 37:37.250
And?

1053
37:37.280 --> 37:38.750
So I decided to show off a little

1054
37:39.130 --> 37:39.710
and said...

1055
37:40.250 --> 37:41.380
they're secretly having an affair.

1056
37:41.610 --> 37:44.280
But I didn't know their wife was sitting nearby,

1057
37:44.750 --> 37:46.230
so they chased me out and kicked me.

1058
37:46.680 --> 37:48.530
Ugh, you deserved that.

1059
37:50.170 --> 37:51.140
Let's go back.

1060
37:51.740 --> 37:53.540
If we're gone too long, Dollar might get suspicious.

1061
37:56.280 --> 37:57.180
What?!

1062
37:57.480 --> 37:58.490
My cast is gone!

1063
38:00.060 --> 38:00.530
Huh?

1064
38:00.950 --> 38:01.600
Oh, no!

1065
38:01.620 --> 38:03.220
Shoot, my cast fell into the water!

1066
38:03.440 --> 38:04.660
Hey, what should we do?

1067
38:04.680 --> 38:05.860
Swim to it.

1068
38:05.880 --> 38:07.060
Hey, are you crazy?

1069
38:07.080 --> 38:08.280
I'm not. Go.

1070
38:08.410 --> 38:09.190
Dolly.

1071
38:10.140 --> 38:11.510
Dolly, where are you?

1072
38:12.030 --> 38:12.910
- I'm screwed. - Dolly!

1073
38:12.930 --> 38:15.090
Dawin, talk to Dollar for me.

1074
38:15.110 --> 38:15.870
Dolly.

1075
38:15.890 --> 38:17.310
Hey, Dolly!

1076
38:19.390 --> 38:20.780
Walk faster, wimpy boy.

1077
38:22.020 --> 38:22.690
Stop.

1078
38:24.170 --> 38:26.280
Auntie Duang calls me "crunchy boy,"

1079
38:26.670 --> 38:27.480
not "wimpy boy."

1080
38:27.690 --> 38:29.410
Well, I'm calling you "wimpy boy."

1081
38:29.610 --> 38:30.930
Why were you on my back?

1082
38:31.270 --> 38:32.470
I meant to help my little brother.

1083
38:33.290 --> 38:35.010
I carried you all this way, thinking the cast was heavy.

1084
38:35.570 --> 38:36.530
I didn't want to ride on your back.

1085
38:40.310 --> 38:40.900
Dawin.

1086
38:41.140 --> 38:41.700
Hm?

1087
38:41.880 --> 38:42.790
Have you seen Dolly?

1088
38:43.850 --> 38:45.010
No, no, I'm completely alone.

1089
38:47.550 --> 38:48.530
That thing floating over there...

1090
38:48.890 --> 38:50.280
looks like Mr. Dolly's cast.

1091
38:51.480 --> 38:52.060
Dolly.

1092
38:52.540 --> 38:53.440
Is he drowning?

1093
38:53.460 --> 38:53.880
Huh?!

1094
38:54.860 --> 38:55.550
- Dolly! - Whoa, whoa!

1095
38:55.570 --> 38:56.950
- No, don't go. - Dolly!

1096
38:56.970 --> 38:58.170
- I'm not letting you go. - Let me go!

1097
38:58.190 --> 38:59.230
- Dolly! - No!

1098
38:59.250 --> 39:00.370
- I'm gonna go help Dolly. - No.

1099
39:01.610 --> 39:03.150
Maybe Dolly didn't fall into the water.

1100
39:03.300 --> 39:04.860
Why is his cast in the pond, then?

1101
39:05.700 --> 39:06.690
I'll help him myself.

1102
39:06.820 --> 39:07.670
Don't!

1103
39:09.060 --> 39:10.680
They are leaping like frogs.

1104
39:11.050 --> 39:12.120
Dolly!

1105
39:12.140 --> 39:13.470
- Never! - What should I do?

1106
39:13.490 --> 39:14.790
- You can't go! - Dolly!

1107
39:20.280 --> 39:21.050
Dolly...

1108
39:21.260 --> 39:21.820
No.

1109
39:23.130 --> 39:23.730
Let me go.

1110
39:26.150 --> 39:27.750
- I can't hold on much longer! - I'm gonna save my brother. Let go!

1111
39:27.770 --> 39:29.270
Dollar, I'm right here!

1112
39:32.060 --> 39:33.020
- Dolly! - Dolly!

1113
39:37.690 --> 39:38.510
- Be careful, okay? - Ow.

1114
39:41.300 --> 39:42.750
Are you alright, Dolly?

1115
39:43.080 --> 39:43.770
Let's go see a doctor.

1116
39:43.790 --> 39:45.480
Hey, it's okay.

1117
39:45.820 --> 39:47.010
I'm alright.

1118
39:47.380 --> 39:48.510
I just slipped and fell into the pond.

1119
39:48.690 --> 39:50.030
Why weren't you being more careful?

1120
39:50.700 --> 39:51.910
How did you even fall into the pond?

1121
39:53.010 --> 39:53.880
Mm...

1122
39:55.980 --> 39:58.090
I was trying to work out.

1123
39:58.380 --> 39:59.050
Huh?

1124
40:00.030 --> 40:02.810
I was sad that I hurt my leg.

1125
40:03.770 --> 40:04.450
Dollar,

1126
40:04.680 --> 40:07.700
I want to work out with you again.

1127
40:09.990 --> 40:12.730
But I guess I'm just unlucky when it comes to working out.

1128
40:12.970 --> 40:16.490
I always get injured every time I try to work out.

1129
40:17.850 --> 40:20.510
I'm so sad...

1130
40:22.290 --> 40:23.230
Don't tell me

1131
40:23.510 --> 40:25.080
him falling into the pond was...

1132
40:26.550 --> 40:27.850
It was all an act.

1133
40:29.500 --> 40:30.550
I see...

1134
40:35.620 --> 40:36.330
Okay,

1135
40:37.080 --> 40:38.930
I won't force you to work out anymore.

1136
40:39.830 --> 40:41.490
That way, you won't get injured like this again.

1137
40:41.510 --> 40:42.750
Really?

1138
40:42.770 --> 40:43.680
Mm.

1139
40:44.270 --> 40:45.350
You promise?

1140
40:46.810 --> 40:47.490
I promise.

1141
40:48.110 --> 40:49.890
Thank you, Dollar.

1142
40:50.940 --> 40:53.050
Oh, I love you so much.

1143
41:01.730 --> 41:03.830
You fell into the pond earlier, right?

1144
41:03.970 --> 41:05.010
That's right.

1145
41:05.150 --> 41:06.930
Why do I smell chlorine instead of mud?

1146
41:11.620 --> 41:13.900
I got out of the water and washed myself.

1147
41:14.060 --> 41:15.260
And your leg is better now?

1148
41:15.730 --> 41:16.680
You can walk normally?

1149
41:17.060 --> 41:17.610
Oh...

1150
41:18.530 --> 41:20.260
It's probably because of the adrenaline.

1151
41:20.280 --> 41:21.690
Now that you mention it...

1152
41:21.890 --> 41:23.550
my leg hurts.

1153
41:24.300 --> 41:25.060
Dawin...

1154
41:25.080 --> 41:25.860
Wrong leg!

1155
41:26.130 --> 41:26.810
Huh?

1156
41:28.830 --> 41:29.500
Oops.

1157
41:30.230 --> 41:31.080
Uh...

1158
41:33.670 --> 41:34.930
Simply put,

1159
41:35.770 --> 41:37.410
I'm sorry!

1160
41:37.950 --> 41:39.270
Dolly...

1161
41:39.290 --> 41:41.400
- Now, now... - You lied to me, huh?

1162
41:41.420 --> 41:43.060
- No, Dollar. - I'm not gonna let this slide!

1163
41:43.080 --> 41:44.530
Where are you going? Come here.

1164
41:45.480 --> 41:47.270
We might need to fetch that cast.

1165
41:47.750 --> 41:49.390
He might really need it after this.

1166
41:50.670 --> 41:51.670
- Hey, Dollar! - Where are you going?

1167
41:51.690 --> 41:53.000
- Dollar! Hey! - Where do you think you're going?

1168
41:53.020 --> 41:53.860
Help me, help.

1169
41:53.880 --> 41:54.490
Where are you going?

1170
41:54.510 --> 41:55.630
I got you.

1171
41:55.650 --> 41:56.590
Hey, Dollar.

1172
41:56.610 --> 41:57.120
Stop running.

1173
41:57.140 --> 41:58.070
- Ow... Hey. - Sit down.

1174
41:58.090 --> 41:59.000
Hold him down.

1175
41:59.020 --> 41:59.860
- Ow, ow. - Don't let him leave.

1176
41:59.880 --> 42:00.710
Why did you do this, hm?

1177
42:00.730 --> 42:02.050
- I didn't mean to. - How many times have you done this?

1178
42:04.020 --> 42:05.530
Dobby...

1179
42:05.990 --> 42:08.900
she actually is not Gaysorn?

1180
42:09.340 --> 42:11.330
My heart is shattered.

1181
42:12.090 --> 42:14.310
It is shattered!

1182
42:14.450 --> 42:15.330
Ugh!

1183
42:15.870 --> 42:16.680
It's annoying!

1184
42:17.700 --> 42:18.380
Huh?

1185
42:20.630 --> 42:21.790
Uh... I mean,

1186
42:22.180 --> 42:23.530
I'm annoyed by these two.

1187
42:24.010 --> 42:25.280
When are you going to tell me

1188
42:25.300 --> 42:26.530
where you got all of this from?

1189
42:27.740 --> 42:28.510
Listen.

1190
42:29.580 --> 42:30.500
Dom

1191
42:31.070 --> 42:33.470
hired me to act paralyzed for 5,000 baht.

1192
42:33.890 --> 42:35.880
He told me to impersonate someone called Gaysorn.

1193
42:36.700 --> 42:38.940
But my real name is Pom.

1194
42:39.310 --> 42:42.350
Ask him about the rest.

1195
42:42.860 --> 42:43.650
I don't know.

1196
42:43.670 --> 42:45.480
Dunno, dunno, dunno...

1197
42:45.650 --> 42:46.300
Dunno, dunno...

1198
42:46.320 --> 42:47.430
Wow, she fell asleep.

1199
42:49.390 --> 42:50.030
Hey.

1200
42:51.450 --> 42:52.950
If you don't want us to press charges,

1201
42:53.180 --> 42:54.350
tell us the truth.

1202
42:54.860 --> 42:57.170
So, you do know the real Grandma Gaysorn, right?

1203
42:57.370 --> 42:59.390
I can't say that I do.

1204
42:59.850 --> 43:02.920
These keepsakes were left behind by the tenant

1205
43:03.070 --> 43:04.520
who lived in my mom's house fifty years ago.

1206
43:04.540 --> 43:05.510
- Huh? - Huh?

1207
43:05.880 --> 43:07.790
Do you know where she lives now?

1208
43:07.810 --> 43:08.280
Yeah.

1209
43:08.710 --> 43:10.170
My mom told me that...

1210
43:11.140 --> 43:12.320
she lived there for a few years

1211
43:12.340 --> 43:14.260
before going back to Bangkok.

1212
43:14.280 --> 43:15.540
And she left these things behind.

1213
43:15.620 --> 43:16.930
I only found them recently, while back on holiday

1214
43:16.950 --> 43:19.540
helping Mom clear out and clean the rental house.

1215
43:21.780 --> 43:22.470
Oh.

1216
43:22.490 --> 43:24.270
She must have been heartbroken

1217
43:24.530 --> 43:26.070
because she left Gramps' love letter

1218
43:26.200 --> 43:28.290
and his photo behind.

1219
43:28.320 --> 43:29.170
True.

1220
43:30.300 --> 43:31.910
He promised to run away with her,

1221
43:32.520 --> 43:33.830
but he never showed up.

1222
43:34.330 --> 43:35.620
Who could blame her for leaving him?

1223
43:49.660 --> 43:50.940
Uh, but...

1224
43:51.340 --> 43:52.680
Since I came all this way

1225
43:52.950 --> 43:55.080
and even brought you Gramps' keepsake,

1226
43:55.530 --> 43:57.480
don't we deserve a little something?

1227
43:58.490 --> 44:00.170
It doesn't have to be five million baht.

1228
44:00.300 --> 44:01.350
5,000 would be enough.

1229
44:01.810 --> 44:03.480
I've got five fingers here. Do you want them?

1230
44:04.150 --> 44:05.020
So fierce...

1231
44:05.340 --> 44:05.880
Hey,

1232
44:06.310 --> 44:09.100
aren't there any of Grandma Gaysorn's photos at that house?

1233
44:13.080 --> 44:14.070
No.

1234
44:14.280 --> 44:14.930
Huh?

1235
44:15.250 --> 44:15.900
Well...

1236
44:16.980 --> 44:19.080
I already told you everything I know.

1237
44:19.870 --> 44:20.610
Now,

1238
44:20.820 --> 44:23.130
will you let Auntie Pom and me

1239
44:23.150 --> 44:24.300
go home already?

1240
44:31.390 --> 44:32.280
Then...

1241
44:32.780 --> 44:34.020
please excuse us.

1242
44:43.080 --> 44:43.830
Auntie Pom.

1243
44:44.170 --> 44:44.770
Auntie Pom!

1244
44:44.790 --> 44:45.710
Let's go.

1245
44:45.830 --> 44:46.990
They allowed us to leave.

1246
44:47.010 --> 44:48.190
Dunno... Dunno...

1247
44:48.210 --> 44:49.350
- Dunno... Dunno... - Ugh.

1248
44:49.370 --> 44:50.570
- Ugh. - Dunno...

1249
44:50.730 --> 44:51.990
Does she even know anything?

1250
44:55.630 --> 44:57.480
I rented this entire costume,

1251
44:57.710 --> 44:59.220
thinking we'd make some progress.

1252
45:00.620 --> 45:01.080
So,

1253
45:01.540 --> 45:02.520
what should we do next?

1254
45:02.660 --> 45:05.880
At the very least, we now know Grandma Gaysorn moved to Bangkok.

1255
45:06.300 --> 45:09.480
She might be closer than we think.

1256
45:09.630 --> 45:10.220
Huh?

1257
45:11.700 --> 45:12.900
Perhaps she is...

1258
45:13.650 --> 45:14.740
- Huh? - under the bed?

1259
45:18.370 --> 45:20.080
I wanted to lighten the mood,

1260
45:20.100 --> 45:21.480
so I cracked a joke.

1261
45:21.730 --> 45:22.660
Ugh...

1262
45:22.680 --> 45:25.080
I think this is just stressing everyone out more.

1263
45:26.740 --> 45:28.010
Just kidding.

1264
45:28.680 --> 45:29.860
Would you like to borrow my watch?

1265
45:29.880 --> 45:31.060
Oh, it is alright.

1266
45:31.080 --> 45:32.510
I do not have the time.

1267
45:36.780 --> 45:39.140
[The D Dorm]

1268
45:39.970 --> 45:45.300
Oh, Danai, why is your life so tragic?

1269
45:45.860 --> 45:51.480
You found true love, yet failed to keep it.

1270
45:52.310 --> 45:58.010
You even made your daughter live in anguish.

1271
45:58.890 --> 46:01.790
You deserved it, old man.

1272
46:01.810 --> 46:03.210
Scritchy-scratchy.

1273
46:04.010 --> 46:04.680
Hey...

1274
46:06.620 --> 46:08.670
Why do you care, huh?

1275
46:08.850 --> 46:10.410
Just go wherever you want.

1276
46:11.020 --> 46:12.290
I want to be alone.

1277
46:12.590 --> 46:13.540
Grandpa,

1278
46:14.090 --> 46:15.330
what has gotten into you, huh?

1279
46:16.050 --> 46:17.880
I am trying to think.

1280
46:19.080 --> 46:22.980
All this time, I have thought of nothing but Gaysorn.

1281
46:23.510 --> 46:24.370
I...

1282
46:25.580 --> 46:27.450
I want to apologize to her,

1283
46:27.740 --> 46:30.850
but I do not know if she...

1284
46:30.870 --> 46:34.120
even wants to hear it.

1285
46:36.170 --> 46:37.080
Oh, Grandpa.

1286
46:37.950 --> 46:39.480
You came all this way,

1287
46:39.900 --> 46:41.080
and now you're chickening out?

1288
46:42.230 --> 46:44.450
My mom and Grandma Gaysorn are really not so different.

1289
46:46.470 --> 46:47.250
Stand tall,

1290
46:47.650 --> 46:48.900
then go apologize to her.

1291
46:50.100 --> 46:52.680
Whether you get yelled at again or she forgives you,

1292
46:53.610 --> 46:54.930
it's better than doing nothing, Grandpa.

1293
47:00.180 --> 47:03.850
Oh, Dobby, what a sweet grandson you are.

1294
47:03.870 --> 47:04.890
Stop it!

1295
47:06.350 --> 47:07.350
Your poems

1296
47:07.580 --> 47:08.930
are always a miss.

1297
47:09.290 --> 47:10.890
Was my great-grandfather Shakespeare or something?

1298
47:11.630 --> 47:12.540
You just keep on composing.

1299
47:14.240 --> 47:14.850
There it is again.

1300
47:17.990 --> 47:18.860
Should I open the door for her?

1301
47:19.200 --> 47:20.240
Will I get hit in the head again?

1302
47:21.870 --> 47:22.530
Alright!

1303
47:23.880 --> 47:24.770
Ow!

1304
47:25.700 --> 47:26.130
Ouch...

1305
47:26.150 --> 47:27.790
Huh? You?

1306
47:27.980 --> 47:29.530
You banged your head on the door again.

1307
47:29.880 --> 47:31.750
- Do you... - Is the door alright?

1308
47:31.770 --> 47:32.610
Ugh.

1309
47:32.630 --> 47:34.030
If it's gonna get me, it's gonna get me.

1310
47:34.050 --> 47:34.530
It hurts...

1311
47:34.680 --> 47:35.610
What do you want?

1312
47:35.630 --> 47:37.350
I have some good news for you.

1313
47:38.360 --> 47:41.500
Deang called to say he recovered the footage from the day Gramps passed.

1314
47:42.050 --> 47:43.060
Now we'll know

1315
47:43.080 --> 47:45.590
who Grandma Gaysorn's relative is in this dorm.

1316
47:53.880 --> 47:54.510
What's wrong?

1317
47:54.530 --> 47:56.260
You don't seem all that happy...

1318
47:56.280 --> 47:57.690
- Are you gonna cry? - I'm glad. I really am.

1319
48:01.650 --> 48:02.650
Are you, though?

1320
48:03.260 --> 48:04.230
I am. I am.

1321
48:18.120 --> 48:18.850
Oh!

1322
48:18.940 --> 48:19.650
I remember now.

1323
48:19.670 --> 48:21.330
They live in Room 407.

1324
48:22.460 --> 48:23.650
Maybe no one's home.

1325
48:25.290 --> 48:26.650
There is not even a single photo.

1326
48:26.760 --> 48:28.290
How would I know

1327
48:28.310 --> 48:30.080
if they are related to Gaysorn?

1328
48:30.100 --> 48:31.370
Danis, have you seen the news?

1329
48:31.390 --> 48:33.440
Our dorm has a dismemberment case. [Locals Terrified! Dismemberment Killer Still at Large]

1330
48:43.830 --> 48:47.270
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

1331
48:47.450 --> 48:51.170
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

1332
48:53.690 --> 48:59.170
♫Every step we take has a meaning♫

1333
49:00.920 --> 49:05.620
♫No path is ever meaningless♫

1334
49:08.100 --> 49:14.240
♫As long as our hearts keep searching♫

1335
49:15.150 --> 49:19.720
♫One day, we'll find what we're yearning for♫

1336
49:19.740 --> 49:23.250
♫Walking alone is fine, but it's better when you're by my side♫

1337
49:23.270 --> 49:26.850
♫It won't be lonely when you're here to walk beside♫

1338
49:26.870 --> 49:30.390
♫Like a love that waits, waits at the D Dorm♫

1339
49:30.410 --> 49:32.760
♫Like a love that remains, remains at the dorm♫

1340
49:32.790 --> 49:39.110
♫Meaningful love and good things await on every path♫

1341
49:39.770 --> 49:46.500
♫It might not be a coincidence that we get to meet♫

1342
49:46.980 --> 49:54.130
♫There might be hidden meanings on the path beneath our feet♫

1343
49:54.150 --> 49:57.310
♫Perhaps the D Dorm is what led me to meet you♫
